W: 2. Oh, my Geordie will be hanged in a golden chain
W: 'Tis not the chain of many
W: He was born of the King's royal breed
W: And lost to a virtuous lady
W:
W: 3. Go bridle me my milk white steed
W: Go bridle me my pony
W: I will ride to London's court
W: To plead the life of Geordie
W:
W: 4. Oh, my Geordie never stole nor cow nor calf
W: He never hurted any
W: He stole sixteen of the king's royal deer
W: And sold them in Bohenny
W:
W: 5. Two pretty babies I have born
W: The third lies in my body
W: I'd freely part them everyone
W: If you'd spare the life of Geordie
W:
W: 6. The looked over his left shoulder
W: He said, fair maid, I'm sorry
W: He said, fair maid, you must be gone
W: For I cannot pardon Geordie
W:
W: 7. Oh, my Geordie will be hanged in a golden chain
